  "scope": [
    "Module SPI as delivered by ST (STM32CubeN6 v1.4.0), FROZEN: the SPI HAL component (classic, handle-based) and the SPI LL component (header-only inline functions) under one functional-level requirement set. The delivered HAL does not use the delivered LL: the two components are parallel public APIs over the same peripheral.",
    "In scope (HAL): initialisation and de-initialisation with their platform hooks; configuration through the initialisation structure (mode, direction, data size, clock polarity and phase, slave-select management, baud-rate prescaler, bit order, TI mode, CRC, FIFO threshold); blocking transmit, receive and transmit-receive; interrupt-driven transmit, receive, transmit-receive and interrupt handling; DMA-driven transmit, receive and transmit-receive; abort, blocking and interrupt-driven; callback registration and unregistration and the transmit/receive/transmit-receive complete, half-complete, error, abort-complete and suspend callbacks; state and error queries.",
    "In scope (LL): enable and disable; configuration (mode, standard, clock polarity and phase, baud-rate prescaler, bit order, transfer direction, data width, slave-select mode and polarity, transfer size, FIFO threshold); master transfer start, suspend and progress; CRC; DMA request enable; interrupt enable and status with the corresponding flags and flag clears; data transmit and receive.",
    "Out of scope (delivered; listed by the governance inventory): the extended HAL services (underrun configuration, I/O configuration lock, receive FIFO flush), DMA pause/resume/stop and the vendor-internal helper functions of the HAL; I2S/PCM mode, slave underrun handling, I/O swap, alternate-function GPIO control and I/O lock, master timing options (inter-data and slave-select idleness, NSS pulse management, receive auto-suspend, FIFO packing), half-duplex direction, internal slave-select level and the DMA register addresses of the LL.",
    "SWE.1 only, at the functional level: register-level detail and concrete negative cases belong to SWE.3."
  ],
